I don't know what the hell it is but I'm on my third contraction of
lycanthropy from wererats on this game. They seem to be relatively
thick on the ground and I've been infected within two bits (given that
it never takes longer to kill them being expert with a unicorn horn).

Anyway, the first time I cured it with a sprig of wolfsbane. The
second time I was in Sokoban, where I'd had to squeeze past a boulder
a while back and forgot I was carrying an unblessed luckstone so when
I prayed to get rid of it, Hermes was displeased. Fabulous. No holy
water because I haven't seen a coaligned alter the whole game and
hadn't been up to killing the minetown priest. And how was I supposed
mollify a displeased god? Not to mention the loss of my 8 points of
protection.

All right, so.... I made my way carefully back to minetown with two
pet large cats, and finally came up with a plan: I would summon lots
of pet rats, line them up in the temple with the priest, and polymorph
them into something hopefully more dangerous, and the priest into
something less. The plan almost didn't work: the priest became a
demilich. But on my second shot with the wand of polymorph, I got a
pet balrog, who killed the priest.

I tried for a while to come up with something sacrificeable, but after
a while I found I couldn't do it. I'd stowed the luckstone, though,
and it had been a while, so I decided to risk prayer. It worked. I was
purified.

So, back at sokoban at last (after guiding a balrog slowly through the
levels, because really, you don't want to lose that pet), I get bit by
another freakin' wererat, feverish on the first bite. Thinking it's
been long enough, knowing I haven't broken any sokoban rules, I pray
again.

Oops. Hermes is displeased. 

All right, well... I think back, and I check the spoiler. Ah. It was
that tin of Gnome Lord meat (I'm a Gnome)... aggravate monster isn't
the only penalty for cannibalism, apparently there's a luck penalty
too.

So I tried stowing the luckstone and waiting this out again -- I
understand if I wait 300-600 turns, I gain a point towards neutral
luck. I waited about 1200 turns, and prayed again, and Hermes was
still displeased.

Can anyone help me out with a good plan here? I clearly don't
understand specifics of luck and divine displeasure well enough here
to time my prayers right (how long would I have to wait to be sure? Is
displeasure the same as anger?). And the other remedies I know
(wolfsbane, holy water) aren't anywhere in sight....  and while I know
stone to flesh,  food is running low and I'm starting to worry that I
might even forget stone to flesh at an inconvenient time....

(P.S. -- I've tried all my rings and none of them are poly control)

